course: dictionary
lesson: 6977
title: Pant
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Pant has more than one meaning, so context tells you which one to use. Read the words around it. «The dog lay in the shade, panting after its walk.» A dog after a walk is hot and tired, so panting means breathing fast and loudly with its mouth open.
explain: Pant can also be a noun, meaning one quick, short breath. «She gave a pant of surprise.» Here pant is a single breath, not breathing for a long time.
explain: Watch out in American books. «He tore his pant leg on the fence.» In US English, pant means trousers. The word leg after it tells you what it means. Always try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: To pant is to breathe fast and loudly, with your mouth open.
fact: You pant when you are hot, tired or excited, for example after running.
fact: Dogs sweat only a little, through their paws, so they cool down mainly by panting.
fact: «The crocodile lying with its mouth wide open cannot sweat, so it lets heat out through its mouth, much as a dog pants.»
fact: «A cheetah can reach about 100 km per hour, but only for about 20 to 30 seconds, then it must rest and lie panting.»
exercise: «The dog lay in the shade, panting after its walk.» What does panting mean here? | Sleeping very deeply | *Breathing fast and loudly with its mouth open | Eating its dinner slowly | Singing a happy song
exercise: «She gave a pant of surprise.» In this sentence, what is a pant? | A long walk up a hill | A pair of trousers | *One quick, short breath | A loud song
exercise: «He tore his pant leg on the fence.» Here pant means: | A fence post | *A pair of trousers | A dog | A wet field
test: Why do dogs pant? | To sing to their owners | *To cool down, because they cannot sweat much | To make the ground warmer | To wash their paws
test: «The cheetah lay panting after its fast run.» What does this show? | It is cold and needs to warm up | They have caught their dinner | It is asleep and dreaming | *Its body needed more oxygen after running hard
exam: Read this: «The runner was panting at the finish line.» Which word is closest in meaning to panting? | Smiling | *Breathing hard | Singing | Shouting
